oeis -- OEIS lookup
*******************

Description
===========

This function looks up the argument (a list of integers or a string) in the
Online Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences (http://oeis.org/).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : oeis {1,3,31,1145}                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = {0 => (A029729 (see https://oeis.org/A029729 ) Degree of the variety of |
|     {1 => (A094579 (see https://oeis.org/A094579 ) Duplicate of A029729.)   |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : NumberedVerticalList                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|pairs of commuting n X n matrices.)}                                         |
|                                   }                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Optional arguments Limit and Position allow to control the maximum amount of
listed answers.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = apply(5,n->n!);                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : oeis (L,Limit=>5)                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {0 => (A000142 (see https://oeis.org/A000142 )                          |
|     {1 => (A072856 (see https://oeis.org/A072856 )                          |
|     {2 => (A061602 (see https://oeis.org/A061602 )                          |
|     {3 => (A177523 (see https://oeis.org/A177523 )                          |
|     {4 => (A263777 (see https://oeis.org/A263777 )                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : NumberedVerticalList                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|Factorial numbers: n! = 1*2*3*4*...*n (                                      |
|Number of permutations satisfying i-4<=                                      |
|Sum of factorials of the digits of n.)                                       |
|Number of permutations of 1..n avoiding                                      |
|Number of inversion sequences avoiding                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|order of symmetric group S_n, number of permutations of n letters).)}        |
|p(i)<=i+4, i=1..n (permutations of length n within distance 4).)    }        |
|                                                                    }        |
| adjacent step pattern up, up, up, up.)                             }        |
|pattern 201 (or 210).)                                              }        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : oeis (L,Limit=>1,Position=>2)                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {0 => (A061602 (see https://oeis.org/A061602 ) Sum of factorials of the |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : NumberedVerticalList                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|digits of n.)}                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use oeis:
=================

  * "oeis(String)"
  * "oeis(VisibleList)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note oeis: oeis, is a *note method function with options:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

